# --concurrent false: the lint-staged globs overlap by design and three
# entries write files another entry also writes. lint-staged defaults to
# running every glob's commands at once, which races them on one file and
# commits whichever write landed last. Serial execution runs them in the
# order package.json declares, which is the order they need:
#
#   1. eslint --fix   (src TS — may rewrap code)
#   2. prettier       (everything — must be last so it formats 1's output)
#   3. permissions generator → docs/spec/api.md (emits Prettier-formatted
#      bytes itself, so it is safe after 2)
#
# CI catches a bad interleaving, but as a confusing red build rather than a
# clean commit.
npx lint-staged --concurrent false
